# What Cloud Build is allowed to see.
#
# This file has to exist. With no .gcloudignore, gcloud generates one that
# inherits .gitignore - and data/deploy is gitignored on purpose, because it is
# a 14.7 MB build artefact reproducible from scripts. The upload would then
# carry no bundle, the image would build cleanly, and create_app() would exit 1
# on a container that never served a request.
#
# It is an allow-list rather than an ignore-list, for the same reason
# scripts/deploy_space.py uses one: a new top-level directory in this
# repository should not reach a public deployment because nobody remembered to
# exclude it.

# Ignore everything at the root, then re-admit only what the image needs.
/*

!/Dockerfile
!/pyproject.toml
!/.dockerignore
!/src
!/scripts
!/data

# Inside data/, only the two directories the Dockerfile copies. data/processed
# alone is 177 MB of embeddings the served path never touches.
/data/*
!/data/manifests
!/data/deploy

# Never, whatever the rules above admit. Later patterns win, so these come last.
.env
*.env
.env.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.key
*.pem
